 "doc": {
  "about": "EIDOLON v5 score + SFX. Original music composed and rendered offline for this project from real instrument samples (see CREDITS.md). Files under res://assets/audio/v5/. _demo.ogg is a listening demo only (not referenced here).",
  "key": "Everything sits in one pitch family: D dorian (D E F G A B C), with Bb only in the darker D-aeolian rooms (stair_breath, garden_veiled, gate_four). Any bed can crossfade into any other.",
  "leitmotif": "Ione's motif A4-D5-E5-F5-E5 (ends unresolved on E). Every room quotes it, varied; solve_* cues finally resolve it (E->D or the room's equivalent); cinematic_hand ends without resolving.",
  "loudness": "Beds and water_lap: -18 LUFS integrated, seamless loops (set AudioStreamOggVorbis.loop = true). Events: -20 LUFS, play at the listed gain_db. solve_*: -17 LUFS. shrine_awaken: -16 LUFS. cinematic_hand: -18 LUFS (dynamic: whispers to swell). glimpse -19, touch_glass -20, breath -21. SFX: mono, normalised per family by short-clip LUFS (footsteps -27, cloth -29, statue_turn / door_stone -20, gate / hollow_scrape -21, scale_creak / shard_pickup -24, rune_flip -25, glass_tap -26, glass_hum -25, ui_click -31), peaks <= -2.5 dBFS; beam_hum loop -24 dBFS RMS. v0.8.1: beds re-rendered softer (per-bed high shelf at 3 kHz -2.5..-11 dB toward a common brightness, 8 kHz low-pass, a slow circular gain ride on swells; loops kept seamless, still -18 LUFS) and played 5.5 dB lower (layer gain_db -5.5, every room the same: the old 0/-1/-2/-3 trims removed); events 3 dB lower and 1.4x sparser.",
  "phone": "All files are high-passed (beds/music: 4th-order 165 Hz) and voiced for phone speakers: fundamentals 180 Hz - 6 kHz, lows carried by harmonics; < 0.5 % energy below 150 Hz.",
  "rooms.layers": "layer 0 = the room bed (loop). Some rooms add the shared water_lap loop as layer 1.",
  "rooms.events": "sparse musical one-shots; pick one at random every min_s..max_s seconds, never the same twice in a row. Each has its own reverb tail baked in.",
  "cues.cinematic_hand": "59 s, through-composed for \"The Hand in the Water\": 0-8 near-silence; 8-16 low strings as she steps closer; 16.5 the hands touch (glass ripple) and the leitmotif emerges; 23-30 her voice sings it; 30-37.6 the veil lifts (swell); 37.6 the whisper = hard cut to silence; 41-59 she walks into the fog, ending on an unresolved Bbmaj7(#11) with her E on top. Start it at the first frame of the cinematic.",
  "cues.extra": {
   "footsteps_wood": "wooden surfaces (4 variants)",
   "door_stone": "heavy stone door / slab sliding, 3-4 s (3 variants)",
   "gate": "iron gate: latch, long creak, settle (3 variants)",
   "glass_tap": "tapping a mirror / glass (5 variants)",
   "glass_hum": "rubbed glass singing, 2.4 s (3 variants)",
   "beam_hum": "Court of Light beam hum, seamless 8 s mono LOOP (replaces set_hum stream)",
   "hollow_scrape": "hollow statue (Kelyfos) dragged / shifting (4 variants)",
   "scale_creak": "the Scales beam creaking (4 variants)",
   "shard_pickup": "picking up a mirror shard (4 variants)",
   "ui_click": "soft stone UI click (4 variants)",
   "rune_flip": "rune tile flip with a glass glint (4 variants)",
   "statue_turn": "rotating statue / plinth, heavy stone grind ~1.5 s (5 variants)",
   "footsteps_stone": "soft stone, wrapped feet (6 variants; randomise pitch +-4 %, level +-2 dB)",
   "footsteps_water": "water's edge (5 variants)",
   "cloth": "cloak / veil swish (5 variants)"
  },
  "cues.solve_jingle": "v0.8.1: the one \"puzzle solved\" jingle, the same motif on every solve (2.3 s, -16 LUFS, reverb baked): a rising plucked-lyre arpeggio D4 F4 A4 D5 E5 F5 A5 that settles on D (krotala/bell shimmer, a soft tympanon and pad swell under it). The music bed ducks -6 dB for ~2 s under it. Original; synthesised offline (tools: scratchpad render_jingle.py, see CREDITS.md)."
